##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# Spec 032, fixture F1 (GiFixture_ICache): a small scene whose render writes a small irradiance cache.
#
# It is sphere-occlusion-reyes (the lone sphere plus an overlapping occluder, occlusion_probe) with the
# cache written to a file: Attribute "irradiance" "handle" names it and "filemode" "w" is
# CACHE_WRITE | CACHE_SAMPLE, so CIrradianceCache writes the tree when the frame ends. maxerror 0.6
# (the default, stated) is greater than zero, so the lookups insert records. 48 x 36 pixels keeps the
# cache to a few hundred records. numthreads 1 (and -t:1 on the command line) fills the cache in a fixed
# order. On the starting tree a cache can only be filled by a render: the insertion there is private to
# CIrradianceCache, or sample() only.
#
# T-A (GiRemote_Loopback*), T-A2 and T-B read the cache this scene writes. The occluder carries
# Attribute "visibility" "diffuse" [1]: ray-visibility categories default OFF (see
# examples/rib/tests/sphere-occlusion-reyes.rib).
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Option "shaderformat" "default" ["rslo"]
Option "limits" "numthreads" [1]
Display "icache-fixture.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 48 36 1
PixelSamples 1 1
Projection "perspective"
Clipping 0.1 100
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
  Attribute "irradiance" "string handle" ["icache-fixture.icache"]
  Attribute "irradiance" "string filemode" ["w"]
  Attribute "irradiance" "float maxerror" [0.6]
  Surface "occlusion_probe"
  Sphere 1 -1 1 360
  AttributeBegin
    Attribute "visibility" "diffuse" [1]
    Surface "matte"
    Translate 1.2 0 -0.5
    Sphere 0.9 -0.9 0.9 360
  AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
